# Model choice, from the benchmark in state/benchmark.md (2026-07-24).
#
# The work model runs a 2h+ agentic loop, so what matters is (a) accurate file:line
# citation, (b) cheap OUTPUT tokens, (c) a big context window so pi's auto-compaction
# fires rarely. deepseek-v4-pro won on all three: every reference it gave checked out
# against source, output is $0.87/M (cheapest of the strong candidates), and 1M context.
#
# COST REGRESSION, 2026-08-15 — unfixed, see RESUME.md. This model's OUTPUT price rose from
# the $0.870/Mtok recorded above to $2.336/Mtok (2.685x) around 2026-08-12. Nothing in the
# rig noticed, because the work is unchanged: the only symptom is that the first pass now
# exhausts the $4.50 work cap on its own and the spend watchdog SIGTERMs it mid-review.
# Between 08-13 and 08-15 that cost 3 charms outright (litmus 80, jimm 82, gatus 84), left
# others accepted-but-truncated with no depth passes and no citation correction, and took
# throughput from 6 reviews/day to 1. A repriced model is a silent quality fault, not an
# outage — the run log looks entirely normal throughout.
#
# DO NOT "fix" this by pinning deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813. Its advertised price in
# OpenRouter's /models listing ($0.435/$0.870) is NOT what it bills: measured against the
# live API on 2026-08-15 it charges $1.320/$3.960 per Mtok, i.e. worse than the alias on
# output. Verify any replacement by billing a real request and reading usage.cost_details,
# never by reading the /models price — they disagree.
#
# So the 2026-07-24 runner-up is promoted instead. Measured live on 2026-08-15:
#   minimax-m2.7      $0.380 in / $1.700 out per Mtok
#   deepseek-v4-pro   $1.131 in / $2.262 out per Mtok
# The loop is heavily input-weighted (a repo re-sent every turn), so on input — the term
# that dominates — m2.7 is ~3x cheaper, which is what brings a run back under the $4.50
# work cap and the day back to 6 charms. It was benchmarked citing perfectly with real tool
# use, which is the quality metric this rig actually depends on.
#
# The cost is context: 205K against deepseek's 1M, so pi's auto-compaction fires far more
# often, and it will fire hardest on exactly the large charms that were failing (litmus
# 48K py_lines, postgresql 42K, kfp 54K at idx 88). That is the thing to check first if
# review quality drops: compare findings count and `citations checked:` against the healthy
# 2026-08-10 baseline (27-34 citations, 12-25 findings), not against the 08-13..15 runs,
# which are all truncated. If it does not hold up, the honest fallback is not another model
# but fewer, bigger slots — cron to */6 with MAX_RUN_BUDGET ~$8.50, ~4 charms/day.
WORK_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m2.7

# Previous work model, kept as the fallback. Still the better model on context (1M) and
# still accurate; it is priced out, not ruled out. If its price comes back down, it should
# come back — re-measure with a billed request before switching.
WORK_MODEL_ALT=deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro

# The editing pass only reads the draft and the notes, so it is a few tens of thousands
# of tokens on an expensive model — affordable, and it is where the writing quality
# comes from.
POLISH_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5

# The weekly cross-charm synthesis is one run a week over the whole corpus of reviews.
# Worth the best model available on this key.
THEMES_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5

# NOT usable on this key:
#   qwen/*        404 "No endpoints available matching your guardrail restrictions and
#                 data policy" — the account's privacy settings would need changing.
#   z-ai/glm-5.2  fails instantly with a provider/auth error.
#   moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code  timed out at 600s having spent $0.65 for no output.
